# radrootsd

This is the README for `radrootsd` which is a long-running daemon for
authenticated publishing and optional NIP-46 control on Rad Roots networks.

NIP-46 kind-24133 request and response events are locally completed through a
dedicated protocol helper and then relayed as already-signed transport
messages. Remote `sign_event` results are accepted only when the author and
canonical event ID match the exact unsigned request and the complete NIP-01
event verifies.

## Verification

`radrootsd --help`, `--version` and subcommand help exit successfully before
loading configuration or creating logging, identity, database or network state.
Malformed arguments retain the redacted nonzero failure boundary.

Run the native standalone checks with the declared Rust toolchain and committed
lockfile. In an extbuild-enabled checkout, first run `cargo extbuild doctor`
and route each command through `cargo extbuild run --`:

```text
cargo fmt --all --check
cargo check --workspace --all-targets --locked
cargo test --workspace --all-targets --locked
cargo clippy --workspace --all-targets --locked -- -D warnings
RUSTDOCFLAGS="-D warnings" cargo doc --workspace --no-deps --locked
scripts/verify-boundaries.sh
scripts/verify-supply-chain.sh
```

The boundary command verifies the source-lock digest against the actual
Cargo.lock and the exact public foundation dependencies resolved offline. It
also byte-compares the root-only public API against its reviewed baseline and
rejects forbidden repository roots or credential material. The supply-chain
command checks the locked dependency, license,
advisory, and immutable public-source policy.

After an intentional dependency-lock update, refresh its digest through the
private owning tool, then check freshness (route these commands through
extbuild in an enabled checkout):

```text
cargo run --locked --offline -p radrootsd_xtask -- source-lock refresh
cargo run --locked --offline -p radrootsd_xtask -- source-lock check
```

The producer verifies the existing typed source-lock schema and actual offline
public dependency graph before atomically replacing only the lockfile digest.
It preserves the selected Lib revision, archive, catalog and version identity;
it does not qualify a new Lib source archive or a release artifact.

The standalone flake exposes exactly one real `radrootsd` package, check, and
application for `aarch64-darwin` and `x86_64-linux`. It exposes no checkout
wrapper, development shell, NixOS module, OCI artifact, or other system.

